{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 9.367,
   "text": "The summer after graduation, my three best friends and I went camping at Pine Hollow."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 9.967,
   "end": 14.425,
   "text": "The old ranger counted us at the gate... and gave us one rule."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 14.925,
   "end": 22.285,
   "text": "If you hear your tent zipper open after the fire's out... don't sit up. Don't turn on a light. Just count heads, in the dark."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 23.285,
   "end": 25.952,
   "text": "We joked about it all through dinner."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 26.452,
   "end": 31.167,
   "text": "Marco kept zipping the tent open and shut, just to make Jess scream."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 31.967,
   "end": 37.577,
   "text": "Then the fire burned down to coals... and the four of us squeezed into one small tent."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 38.777,
   "end": 43.257,
   "text": "Sometime after two, I woke up. Everyone was breathing slow."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 44.057,
   "end": 48.345,
   "text": "And then I heard it. The zipper. Opening... one tooth at a time."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 50.945,
   "end": 57.409,
   "text": "Cold air slid across my face. Something crawled in... and lay down, very carefully, beside me."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 58.609,
   "end": 62.471,
   "text": "I didn't sit up. I reached out in the dark, and counted."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 63.271,
   "end": 65.895,
   "text": "Jess. Marco. Tyler. Me."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 66.895,
   "end": 70.585,
   "text": "Four. Everyone was here. Everyone was asleep."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 71.985,
   "end": 76.209,
   "text": "Then, right beside my ear... a soft voice kept counting."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 78.009,
   "end": 78.889,
   "text": "Five."
  }
 ],
